From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:48:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 26/26] book ch.19: nested sampling plans from variance
 components (Case Study 19.3)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- core/stats/sampling.py: sampling_scheme_power — RCBD with n_R blocks
  and n_T treatments on experimental units plus nested sub-samples: dummy
  ANOVA with predicted stratum variances and df (Table 19.4), SE and SED
  of treatment means, power for a difference δ (chapter 10 machinery),
  comparison of several schemes, 10–20 residual df rule warning.
- New "planning" bridge kind (method without data columns).
- Tests against Table 19.4b and pp. 534–535; the book's alternative-scheme
  variances (0.0186, 0.0355) do not follow its own formula (0.0140,
  0.0171) — its powers are reproduced from its variances.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
